summary:
  A DLNA Stop answered with any HTTP error is reported as stopped.

history:
  An idle renderer answers Stop with a SOAP fault, and that is a quiet DONE.
  The handler took every HTTP error for one. A fault rides HTTP 500; a 404
  (the control address is gone) or a 503 (busy) is not the renderer speaking
  about Stop at all, and the widget said nothing while the speaker may have
  gone on playing. Measured 2026-11-10 against a local server answering 404,
  500 and 503: DONE all three times.

target:
  package/contents/ui/cast.py

find:
          if exc.code != 500:

replace:
          if exc.code >= 600:

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cast_stop.py::test_cmd_dlna_stop_refused_at_the_door_emits_fail.
  Line-neutral.
